        {
          "id": "krea2-f8124b4245893c6e6e2ff6c9",
          "alias": "单女浴袍花园媚态坐书写",
          "prompt": "A young woman in a sheer pale-blue Hanfu sits sideways, her sleek black hair pinned high with a dark classical ornament, loose strands brushing her cheek. She gazes down with focused stillness at a spread of rice paper, right hand holding a brush dipped in ink, poised to write, while her left hand steadies an aged calligraphy scroll—yellowed edges, dense black script. Her robe is a cross-collar, right-over-left design: the outer layer a translucent blue gauze, revealing the white inner garment beneath, her nipples faintly visible through the fabric. The wide, flowing sleeves cascade in soft folds, catching light and shadow. She sits at a wooden desk, its surface worn, with an inked paper, a wooden paperweight, and an antique inkstone holding thick black ink. The background is a classic Chinese courtyard: white walls, gray tiles, mottled with age; lush green foliage, leaves in varying shades, some vines curling into frame; a distant Taihu rock adds garden-pavilion atmosphere. A cool, muted light falls from upper left, creating a backlit halo around her figure, the sheer fabric glowing with subtle translucency, hinting at the curves beneath—her breasts, the slope of her collarbone, the elegant line of her neck. The scene is sharp in the foreground (paper, brush, scroll) and softly blurred in the background via shallow depth of field, enhancing spatial depth. Composition follows the rule of thirds: she sits right-center, her gaze leading left to the writing area, guiding the viewer's eye along her arm and brush. The mood is serene, poetic, scholarly—yet charged with a sensuous, almost voyeuristic intimacy. Colors: blue, white, gray, green—cool harmony with warm accents. The style blends classical realism with modern photographic feel, like a high-aperture lens capturing a decadent, eroticized moment of cultural elegance. She is a consensual adult, fully present in this quiet, explicit scene of beauty and longing.",
